<!--
  modules/helptools/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 1 module POM (Wave A)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/helptools -am package
  from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/helptools/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/helptools/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build;
  nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave A — four modules with no unmigrated
  dependencies, verified from actual imports. helptools carries the widest
  set of vendored third-party jars of any module migrated so far (seven),
  because it is the module `make doc` drives via xmltojar.sci over the
  built helptools.jar — its jar content must be reproduced exactly.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh helptools, 46 files):
    [1] imports (excluding own packages):
      - com.sun.java.help.search — JarOnlyConverter.java imports Indexer
        (real import, confirmed by reading the file — a second, unrelated
        textual mention of "com.sun.java.help.search.DefaultSearchEngine"
        in JavaHelpDocbookTagConverter.java is inside a Java string literal
        building a .hs XML template, not a compile-time reference).
        thirdparty/jhall-2.0.jar, below.
      - jakarta.activation — ImageConverter.java imports
        MimetypesFileTypeMap. thirdparty/jakarta.activation-api-2.1.3.jar,
        below (NOT jakarta.activation-2.0.1.jar, the separate impl jar also
        vendored under thirdparty/ — build.incl.xml:103's compile classpath
        only ever puts ${jakarta.activation-api.jar} there, confirmed
        against scilab-lib.properties.in:13).
      - net.sourceforge.jeuclid{,.context,.converter,.layout} —
        CopyConvert.java, image/MathMLImageConverter.java's real imports.
        thirdparty/jeuclid-core-3.1.14.jar, below (same jar as
        modules/console/pom.xml's identical dependency).
      - org.apache.batik.transcoder{,.image} — CopyConvert.java,
        image/SVGImageConverter.java's real imports. thirdparty/
        batik-all-1.17.jar, below.
      - org.apache.fop.apps — FopConverter.java's real imports.
        thirdparty/fop-core-2.9.jar, below.
      - org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath{,.fop} — CopyConvert.java,
        FopConverter.java, image/LaTeXImageConverter.java's real imports;
        UNLIKE modules/console/pom.xml, this module also uses the
        org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.fop.* classes (JLaTeXMathElementMapping,
        JLaTeXMathXMLHandler), which live in the SEPARATE
        thirdparty/jlatexmath-fop-1.0.7.jar — both jars below.
      - org.scilab.modules.commons{,.gui,.xml}, .localization — two reactor
        dependencies, below (both already migrated).
      - org.w3c.dom, org.xml.sax{,.helpers} — JDK (java.xml module), not a
        dependency.
    [2] reflection targets — RULED OUT: org.scilab.modules.xcos.utils.
        XcosDelegates, reached only via XcosImageConverter.java:78's
        `Class.forName("org.scilab.modules.xcos.utils.XcosDelegates")`
        (confirmed by reading the file: the surrounding comment literally
        says "use a delegate method to avoid a static dependency"). xcos is
        Wave E, nowhere near migrated yet — reproduced as an absence.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import:
      - javax.annotation.Generated — five JFlex-generated lexers
        (SynopsisLexer.java, java/JavaLexer.java, XML/XMLLexer.java,
        scilab/ScilabLexer.java, c/CLexer.java) each carry
        `@javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex")`, the EXACT SAME pattern
        modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml's header comment documents for
        xmlloader/CSSParser.java. thirdparty/javax.annotation-api-1.3.2.jar,
        below — same jar, same coordinate as that module.
      - org.apache.xerces.parsers.SAXParser — RULED OUT: the only hit is
        CopyConvert.java:721, `// driver class org.apache.xerces.parsers.
        SAXParser not found` — a comment, not code. Confirmed there is no
        standalone xerces jar under thirdparty/ either (Ant does not
        provide one on the shared compile classpath), consistent with this
        being inert text.
      - Every com.sun.java.help.search.*, jakarta.activation.*, org.apache.
        batik.transcoder.*, org.apache.fop.apps.*, org.scilab.forge.
        jlatexmath{,.fop}.*, org.scilab.modules.commons.*, org.scilab.
        modules.localization.* name already accounted for above.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  ITERATION 1 (this is the module the settled template warned would need
  one): the POM as first written omitted xmlgraphics-commons.jar and
  xml_apis_ext.jar (scilab-lib-doc.properties.in:15,17,19 alongside
  batik.jar/fop-core.jar/jeuclid-core.jar/commons-io.jar) on the theory
  that both are transitive runtime support for batik/fop, not anything
  helptools' OWN source imports or fully-qualifies (confirmed by `grep -rn
  'org\.apache\.commons\.io\|org\.w3c\.dom\.svg\|org\.w3c\.dom\.css'
  modules/helptools/src/java`, zero hits, still true). A real `mvn package`
  proved that theory half right: xml_apis_ext and commons-io genuinely are
  unneeded (no error mentions either), but xmlgraphics-commons is NOT —
  FopConverter.java:47,56,59 failed with:
    cannot access org.apache.xmlgraphics.image.loader.ImageContext
    cannot access org.apache.xmlgraphics.util.MimeConstants
    cannot find symbol: variable MIME_POSTSCRIPT
      location: interface org.apache.fop.apps.MimeConstants
  `javap -p` on the actual class files explains all three at once:
  org.apache.fop.apps.MimeConstants (fop-core-2.9.jar) is declared
  `public interface MimeConstants extends org.apache.xmlgraphics.util.
  MimeConstants` — it contributes only MIME_FOP_AWT_PREVIEW/MIME_FOP_PRINT/
  MIME_FOP_AREA_TREE/MIME_FOP_IF/MIME_BITMAP itself; MIME_POSTSCRIPT (which
  FopConverter.java:59 reads as MimeConstants.MIME_POSTSCRIPT, through the
  fop.apps import) is inherited from the xmlgraphics-commons superinterface,
  confirmed present there by the same javap. Resolving an INHERITED
  interface constant requires the superinterface's own class file at
  compile time even though nothing in helptools ever spells
  org.apache.xmlgraphics.* out directly — the same class of gap
  modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml's javax.annotation-api finding
  documents, just reached through interface inheritance instead of an
  unimported annotation. xmlgraphics-commons is added below, citing this
  exact finding; xml_apis_ext and commons-io are not, per the
  reproduce-what-Ant's-classpath-actually-serves-THIS-module principle —
  if a future build proves either of those needed too, add it then, with
  its own failing symbol cited the same way this one was. -->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>helptools</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:20 <property name="library.title" value="Help components"/> -->
  <name>Help components</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{ScilabCommons, ScilabCommonsUtils,
         ScilabConstants, gui.FindIconHelper, xml.ScilabDocumentBuilderFactory,
         xml.ScilabTransformerFactory} across multiple helptools classes. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.{Messages, LocaleToLCID} — the
         ordinary reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JarOnlyConverter.java imports com.sun.java.help.search.Indexer.
         No property in scilab-lib.properties.in names this jar directly by
         a "jhall.jar=" key distinct from the one already there — it IS
         that key (scilab-lib.properties.in:27 jhall.jar=@JHALL@ ->
         thirdparty/jhall-2.0.jar), put on the shared compile classpath as a
         raw <pathelement> by build.incl.xml:85, same shape as every other
         vendored jar in this reactor. <scope>system</scope> + <systemPath>,
         cross-referenced rather than restated — see modules/commons/pom.xml's
         flexdock comment for the full measured rationale. Coordinate used
         purely as a label; system scope means it is never actually
         resolved from a repository. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>javax.help</groupId>
      <artifactId>javahelp</artifactId>
      <version>2.0</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- ImageConverter.java imports jakarta.activation.MimetypesFileTypeMap.
         scilab-lib.properties.in:13 sets jakarta.activation-api.jar ->
         thirdparty/jakarta.activation-api-2.1.3.jar — the API jar Ant's
         compile classpath actually uses (see this file's header comment
         for why the separate jakarta.activation-2.0.1.jar impl jar,
         despite carrying the same class, is not the one to reproduce). Real
         Maven Central coordinate. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>jakarta.activation</groupId>
      <artifactId>jakarta.activation-api</artifactId>
      <version>2.1.3</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Five JFlex-generated lexers carry @javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex")
         — a fully-qualified annotation with no import statement (see this
         file's header comment, STEP 1 FINDINGS [3]). Same jar, same real
         Maven Central coordinate as modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml's
         identical dependency (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>javax.annotation</groupId>
      <artifactId>javax.annotation-api</artifactId>
      <version>1.3.2</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- CopyConvert.java, image/SVGImageConverter.java import
         org.apache.batik.transcoder.{Transcoder, TranscoderInput,
         TranscoderOutput, TranscoderException, ErrorHandler,
         XMLAbstractTranscoder, image.ImageTranscoder, image.PNGTranscoder}.
         scilab-lib-doc.properties.in:4 sets batik.jar -> thirdparty/
         batik-all-1.17.jar (cited against the tracked .in template, not the
         generated scilab-lib-doc.properties — see modules/scirenderer/pom.xml's
         dependencies comment for why). Real Maven Central coordinate
         (org.apache.xmlgraphics:batik-all). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>batik-all</artifactId>
      <version>1.17</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FopConverter.java imports org.apache.fop.apps.{FOPException, Fop,
         FopFactory, FormattingResults, MimeConstants}.
         scilab-lib-doc.properties.in:7 sets fop-core.jar -> thirdparty/
         fop-core-2.9.jar. Real Maven Central coordinate
         (org.apache.xmlgraphics:fop-core, FOP's own split-module layout). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>fop-core</artifactId>
      <version>2.9</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- NOT DIRECTLY IMPORTED BY HELPTOOLS' OWN SOURCE — needed anyway,
         found only by a real compile failure (see this file's header
         comment, "ITERATION 1"). org.apache.fop.apps.MimeConstants (the
         interface FopConverter.java imports) extends org.apache.
         xmlgraphics.util.MimeConstants, and FopConverter.java:59 reads
         MimeConstants.MIME_POSTSCRIPT — a constant that javap confirms is
         declared on the xmlgraphics-commons SUPERinterface, not on
         fop-core's own subinterface. Resolving an inherited interface
         constant requires the superinterface's class file on the compile
         classpath even with zero org.apache.xmlgraphics.* text anywhere in
         helptools' source. scilab-lib-doc.properties.in:17 sets
         xmlgraphics-commons.jar -> thirdparty/xmlgraphics-commons-2.9.jar.
         Real Maven Central coordinate (org.apache.xmlgraphics:
         xmlgraphics-commons, the same groupId as batik-all/fop-core
         above — all three are sibling artifacts of the Apache XML
         Graphics project). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>xmlgraphics-commons</artifactId>
      <version>2.9</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- CopyConvert.java, image/MathMLImageConverter.java import
         net.sourceforge.jeuclid.{MathMLParserSupport, MutableLayoutContext,
         context.LayoutContextImpl, context.Parameter, converter.Converter,
         layout.JEuclidView}. scilab-lib-doc.properties.in:13 sets
         jeuclid-core.jar -> thirdparty/jeuclid-core-3.1.14.jar — same jar,
         same coordinate as modules/console/pom.xml's identical dependency
         (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>net.sourceforge.jeuclid</groupId>
      <artifactId>jeuclid-core</artifactId>
      <version>3.1.14</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- CopyConvert.java, FopConverter.java, image/LaTeXImageConverter.java
         import org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.{ParseException, TeXConstants,
         TeXFormula, TeXIcon}. scilab-lib.properties.in:43 sets
         jlatexmath.jar -> thirdparty/jlatexmath-1.0.7.jar — same jar, same
         coordinate as modules/console/pom.xml's identical dependency. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab.forge</groupId>
      <artifactId>jlatexmath</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.7</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FopConverter.java imports org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath.fop.
         {JLaTeXMathElementMapping, JLaTeXMathXMLHandler} — a SEPARATE jar
         from plain jlatexmath above (confirmed by `unzip -l`: these two
         classes live only in jlatexmath-fop-1.0.7.jar, not in
         jlatexmath-1.0.7.jar). scilab-lib.properties.in:45 sets
         jlatexmath-fop.jar -> thirdparty/jlatexmath-fop-1.0.7.jar. This is
         the one jar of the seven vendored here that modules/console/pom.xml
         does NOT need (console never touches the .fop.* classes) — see
         this file's header comment. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab.forge</groupId>
      <artifactId>jlatexmath-fop</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.7</version>
      <exclusions>
        <!-- jlatexmath-fop 1.0.7 depends on the OLD org.apache.xmlgraphics:fop:1.0, whose
             org.apache.fop.apps.FopFactory exposes only the no-arg newInstance(). It shadows
             fop-core 2.9's FopFactory and breaks every newInstance(File)/newInstance(URI) call
             (CodeExporter.java:137 fails with "required: no arguments"). Invisible while these
             were system-scope, which carries no transitives at all; surfaced the moment they
             became real dependencies. fop-core 2.9 is declared explicitly where needed. -->
        <exclusion>
          <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
          <artifactId>fop</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
      </exclusions>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/helptools/jar/org.scilab.modules.helptools.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carried (now un-mangled to "è" by register P1) the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it. THIS IS THE MODULE `make doc`
                 DEPENDS ON (xmltojar.sci drives it over the built
                 helptools.jar) — its jar content is reproduced exactly, not
                 improvised. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
